#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * Turn `qlty smells` into a verdict.
 *
 * `qlty smells` exits 0 whether it finds twelve problems or none, and smells do
 * not participate in `qlty check` - not with `[smells] mode = "block"`, not
 * with an inline `qlty-ignore` comment, not with an `[[exclude]]` block and not
 * with `[[triage]] set.ignored`. All four were tried; all four are
 * linter-pipeline machinery that `qlty smells` never consults. So the gate is
 * here, and so is the list of findings this project has looked at and kept.
 *
 * The rule is default-deny. Every finding qlty reports must match an entry in
 * KEPT below, or this exits 1. A new duplication, a new complex function, and
 * any smell nobody has seen yet - boolean logic, nesting, parameter counts -
 * all fail without anyone having to remember to add them here first.
 *
 *   bin/qlty-smells-gate            # the whole tree
 *   bin/qlty-smells-gate --quiet    # only what fails
 *
 * The findings are keyed by what does not move when the code around them does:
 *
 *   Duplication carries a `structural_hash` from qlty - derived from the syntax
 *   tree, so it survives reformatting and renaming a line above it. One hash
 *   covers every end of a cluster. Change what the duplicated code DOES and the
 *   hash changes, which is the point: the pair was kept on the strength of an
 *   argument about that code, and the argument has to be made again.
 *
 *   A hash alone is not enough, which was measured rather than assumed: paste a
 *   THIRD copy of a kept pair and qlty reports the same hash, "in 3 locations",
 *   and a hash-only gate waves it through. So each entry also records how many
 *   copies were agreed to, and a further one fails.
 *
 *   Complexity carries no hash, so it is keyed by rule, file and the symbol
 *   qlty names, plus the count it was accepted at. Growth past that count
 *   fails. Equality would fail every innocent refactor; no bound at all would
 *   let `health.ts` go from 87 to 300 in silence, which is exactly the failure
 *   the old blanket exclusion was criticised for.
 */
import { spawnSync } from "node:child_process";

/**
 * Every finding on this tree that has been looked at and deliberately kept.
 *
 * Adding an entry is a decision, not a formality. It says the code is right and
 * the measurement is wrong about it, or that the finding belongs to somebody
 * else. Each one carries the argument, because an unexplained entry is the one
 * a future contributor copies.
 */
const KEPT = [
  // ---- Duplication -------------------------------------------------------
  {
    hash: "f0b5b555e25dd5702f2c4cd4a2bf8faf",
    locations: 2,
    where: "src/ui/disclosure-bar.tsx / src/ui/landed/landed-lens.tsx",
    why:
      "`NothingOmitted` and `NothingLanded`: the same empty state, telling " +
      "'unreadable' apart from 'genuinely empty', under different labels. " +
      "Sharing them would put one component in front of two bands that are " +
      "still moving, and the wrong shared component is more expensive than " +
      "the duplication. Recorded 2026-08-31 in " +
      "docs/decisions/2026-08-31-what-the-parallel-lens-build-duplicated.md.",
  },
  {
    hash: "3509ebfb6b466865bc21d0d3b40a68ac",
    locations: 2,
    where: "src/ui/deck/deck-row.tsx / src/ui/needs-you/decision-card.tsx",
    why:
      "The 'Blocked by' block, drawn in two bands that answer different " +
      "questions - what the fleet is handling by itself, and what is held " +
      "for a person. The two were deliberately not merged so that a restyle " +
      "of one band does not land in the other. Same record as above.",
